  "body": "In section 4.14. Common idioms without dedicated elements there is [section about the main part of the content](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics-other.html#the-main-part-of-the-content). It offers several ways to mark up main content (not do it at all, use `section` etc.).\r\n\r\nHowever #3354 caused that now main part of the content has its own dedicated element, [`main`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/grouping-content.html#the-main-element):\r\n\r\n> The `main` element represents the dominant contents of the document.\r\n\r\nSection 4.14.1 seems obsolete after this change. Shouldn't it be removed?",
